From 2a1c64bac4d95e93b601221a5b4dacfc3d6285d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Macnak <natsu@google.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:32:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 31/42] Hide transfer only queues when ASTC and ETC2 emulation
 enabled

Gfxstream supports ASTC emulation by inspecting `vkCmdPipelineBarrier()`
calls and inserting extra commands into the provided command buffers to
dispatch compute shaders. Gfxstream, however, does not control which
queues these command buffers are submitted to so we must hide
transfer-only queues to ensure compute shader work is not scheduled on
transfer-only queues.

Bug: b/571544769
Test: dEQP-VK.api.copy_and_blit.copy_commands2.image_to_image_transfer_queue.all_formats.color.2d_to_1d.etc2_r8g8b8_unorm_block.r16g16b16a16_unorm#optimal_optimal
Low-Coverage-Reason: full dEQP not running in CI yet so no coverage
Change-Id: I581cfc597f5b869f0c7f9e9107e3f118bb03369c
(cherry picked from commit bf62e4b7b4ab2449fba448a38a733ea5396be533)
[MAS: resolved against the local ANDROID_EMU_VK_ASTC_BC3 change in
 initFeatures(), and kept logging the ASTC and ETC2 emulation settings
 there, now read from the members setFeatures() fills in. The emulator
 has to set VulkanAstcEmulation and VulkanEtc2Emulation, or both
 emulations are off (ModAVD/ModAVD#39).]

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#39
